{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1794235721","published":"2026-11-09T14:48:59Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:17:20.647915274Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-2004"],"summary":"Fix of 16 CVEs","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: type confusion in selectivity estimators.\n     Any user who can create an operator could attach a selectivity\n     estimator that assumes particular data types, such as intarray's\n     _int_matchsel, to an operator on other data types; the planner then\n     treated a query value as a pointer, so the user could crash the\n     server and possibly run code in it.\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-2004.patch: require superuser to attach a\n       selectivity estimator that is not built in, make tsmatchsel, the\n       inet estimators and intarray's _int_matchsel check the data types\n       they are given, and add the pg_extension OID syscache that the\n       intarray check needs (upstream 9fa38c572a, ea3bf34986, 7e82d9a04d).\n       Also fix a statistics cache reference leak in _int_matchsel\n       (upstream a96b051a98, no CVE).\n     - BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: a non-superuser can no longer CREATE OPERATOR or\n       ALTER OPERATOR ... SET with a RESTRICT or JOIN estimator that is\n       not built in, including those of contrib modules such as intarray\n       and ltree, so restoring a dump that creates such an operator now\n       fails unless done by a superuser.  Superusers, extension scripts\n       and existing operators are not affected, except that networksel\n       and networkjoinsel now raise an error when attached to any operator\n       other than the inet ones.\n     - CVE-2026-2004","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libecpg-compat3","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:18.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libecpg-compat3?distro=ubuntu-18.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"10.23-0ubuntu0.18.04.2+tuxcare.els14"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu18.0